Implement Truly Atomic Database Writes for Workout Generation

The current workout generation system writes to the database incrementally throughout the process (programmed workouts, workout stages, programmed exercises, set schemes), which can leave the database in an inconsistent state if the process fails partway through.

Requirements:
1. Collect all workout data first - Generate all workout stages, exercises, and set schemes in memory without writing to the database
2. Write everything atomically - Use a single database transaction to write all data at once
3. Maintain existing functionality - All current workout generation logic should work the same way
4. Ensure unit tests pass - Update any tests that depend on the current incremental approach

Technical Approach:
1. Create data classes to hold all workout generation data (workout stages, exercises, set schemes) before database writes
2. Modify the workout generation services to collect data instead of writing immediately
3. Create a new atomic writer service that takes all collected data and writes it in a single transaction
4. Update the main workout generation flow to use the new atomic approach
5. Ensure all unit tests are updated and passing

Key Files to Modify:
- ConjugateWorkoutGeneratorService.kt - Main orchestration
- WorkoutStageGenerationOrchestrator.kt - Stage generation coordination
- WorkoutStageGenerationService.kt - Individual stage generation logic
- ThreeDayWorkoutStageGenerationService.kt - 3-day workout logic
- TwoDayWorkoutStageGenerationService.kt - 2-day workout logic
- FourDayWorkoutStageGenerationService.kt - 4-day workout logic
- All related test files

Success Criteria:
- All database writes happen in a single atomic transaction
- If any part of workout generation fails, no partial data is written to the database
- All existing unit tests pass
- No changes to the public API or user experience